                            <h2 style="text-align: center; text-decoration: underline;">Instructions to the Candidates</h2>
                            <table>
                                <tr>
                                    <td colspan="2" style="padding: 10px;">
                                        1.  Admission to the test venue will be on production of this admit card along with your original photo Identity proof and one self-attested photocopy of that ID Proof (like Driving License/ Voter Card/ Aadhar Card/ Passport etc.). The examination will start as per the schedule given in the admit card.
                                        <br>  <br>
                                        2. The admission to the test room will be allowed only 30 Min before the scheduled time. No candidate will be allowed to the examination hall after 15 minutes of the commencement of the test and will also not be allowed to leave the examination hall till the test is over.
                                        <br><br>
                                        3.  Applicants who appear to be prima facie eligible are provisionally permitted to sit for the examination. If after scrutiny at any stage, it is found that the candidate is otherwise ineligible his candidature will be automatically cancelled, even if he has appeared at the examination and secured a position in the merit.

                                        <br><br>
                                        4. You should compulsorily hand over the OMR Answer sheet and question papers to Invigilator after completion of examination.
                                        <br><br>
                                        5.  At the test center you are expected to maintain discipline. Thus interchanging seats, creating disturbance, exchanging notes, consulting/ talking to each other, seeking/ receiving any help from external means etc. will result in cancellation of your candidature for the post.
                                        <br><br>
                                        6.  Mobile phone, pager, electronic calculator, test booklet, notes, scales and logarithm table shall not be permitted during the test. You have to make your own arrangement to keep these items out of the premises of the test venues.
                                        <br><br>
                                        7.  Candidates resorting to any kind of unfair means will be disqualified.  <br><br>
                                        8.  You must ensure that your signature and invigilator’s signature are put (in the space provided for it) on the Admit Card & attendance sheet, failing which the Candidate will be treated as absent.
                                        <br><br>
                                        9.  Please quote your 6 digit Roll number as a reference for any future communication and keep a photocopy with you as this admit card will be collected from you during the examination.
                                        <br><br>
                                        10. This Admit card issued to you is on the basis of information furnished by you on your application form. Your candidature for the post applied will be subject to your fulfilling the eligibility criteria stipulated in the detailed Advertisement available on the website <a href="#"> www.hindustancopper.com</a>.
                                        <br><br>
                                        11. Please note that this letter does not constitute an offer of appointment to you.
                                        <br><br>
                                        12. Strictly follow the instructions given by the Center Supervisor / Room invigilator and those given on the question booklet.
                                        <br><br>
                                        13. No travelling expenses will be admissible for appearing in the written test
                                        <br><br>
                                        14.    The Duration of Test is 2 hours. All questions will be of multiple choices. The written test will consists of two parts. Details are given below: -
